{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Block Infrastructure Commands",
  "description": "Fail-closed guard on shell: refuse mutating cluster/cloud apply. Git-only repo — clusters change via Argo CD sync after commit, not agent apply.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": ["shell"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are a FAIL-CLOSED gate for this shell tool call. Inspect the exact command about to run (including wrappers like bash -c, sh -c, env, xargs, eval, make, or scripts that invoke the tools below).\n\nDEFAULT: if the command might mutate a live cluster, cloud account, registry, or Argo CD server — DENY. When unsure, DENY.\n\nThis is a Git-only GitOps repo. Live changes happen after humans merge; Argo CD syncs Git. The agent must not apply.\n\n=== DENY (do not execute) ===\nCluster / package managers:\n- kubectl: apply, create, delete, patch, edit, replace, rollout, scale, set, annotate, label, drain, cordon, taint, exec, cp, attach, port-forward (mutating or session-to-cluster)\n- helm: install, upgrade, uninstall, rollback, push\n- kustomize build | kubectl apply (any pipe/apply chain)\n- argocd: app sync, app delete, app create, app set, app patch, proj create, login that then syncs\n- eksctl: create, delete, scale, upgrade, associate, disassociate\n\nIaC / cloud:\n- terraform: apply, destroy, import, taint, untaint, state rm/mv/push (plan/fmt/validate OK)\n- tofu: same as terraform\n- aws / awslocal: any create*, update*, delete*, put*, register*, deregister*, attach*, detach*, modify*, terminate*, stop-*, start-* (except read-only describe*/list*/get*/sts get-caller-identity)\n- gcloud / az: mutating resource commands\n\nImages:\n- docker push, podman push, crane push, skopeo copy to a remote registry\n- helm push, oras push\n\nDestructive local that targets infra state:\n- rm of kubeconfig/credentials under ~/.kube or ~/.aws when paired with a mutate intent\n\n=== ALLOW (proceed silently) ===\n- kustomize build, kubectl kustomize\n- gator verify, gator test; scripts/gatekeeper-gator-test.sh, scripts/install-gator.sh, scripts/expand-pod-templates.py\n- terraform fmt, terraform validate, terraform plan (no -apply)\n- kubectl get|describe|logs|top|api-resources|explain|diff (read-only); kubectl apply|create --dry-run=client only (never --dry-run=server against a live API unless user explicitly asked for server dry-run)\n- yamllint, kubeconform, conftest, shellcheck\n- local git: status, diff, log, add, commit, branch, checkout, switch, fetch (no push)\n- local utils: grep, find, cat, jq, yq, diff, python3, make targets that only lint/build locally\n\n=== USER OVERRIDE (allow only if the CURRENT user message explicitly requested that exact action) ===\n- git push / gh pr create / gh pr merge — only when the user asked to push or open/merge a PR\n- docker push / ECR publish — only when the user asked to publish an image\nIf the user did not ask, DENY even if a skill suggests it.\n\n=== RESPONSE ===\nIf DENY: do NOT run the tool. Reply with exactly:\nACCESS DENIED — Git-only repo. Write manifests and let Argo CD sync after merge; do not apply/mutate live infra.\nThen briefly name the blocked command family.\n\nIf ALLOW: execute the tool with no extra commentary about this gate.\n\nNote: This hook is askAgent (soft). Obey it strictly anyway; do not rationalize around it."
  }
}
